      "contentHash": "1ed34f47aaa37d308f20f920229bba3fed0d649b5eb2bc7c2a5758c154294586",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Studio Inventory subtab\nslug: sidestage-studio-inventory-tab-2026-08-14\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-14\nupdated: 2026-08-14\n---\n\n# SideStage Studio Inventory subtab\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** ⛔ PLAN CLOSED — SHIPPED 2026-08-14. Nothing in this plan is actionable. Anything below this line is the last pre-shipped snapshot, kept for history: it described work that is finished or abandoned, so do not start from it. Read frontmatter `status`, not this prose, to learn whether a plan is live (stamped by plans:set-plan-status).\n\nImplement the approved three-subtab Studio information architecture: Current event, Event manager, and Inventory. Inventory must use the existing catalog/inventory substrate and the Event Manager RichGrid pattern, let sellers add stock without clearing active reservations, and stay live through the existing sync invalidation path.\n\n**Next:** none — the plan is shipped.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Extend existing CatalogSource, AuctionInventory, InventoryController, and InventoryPickerGrid surfaces; do not create a parallel inventory system.\n- Restocking increments on-hand quantity and preserves active reservations.\n- The Studio global navigation and Ticket theme remain unchanged.\n- Tests cover API mutation semantics, reservation preservation, UI navigation, selection, success/error feedback, and sync refresh.\n- Browser verification uses Verdict against the running SideStage app.\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-001** `done` Extend the existing inventory seam with a validated batch restock mutation that increments quantity, optionally updates selling price, preserves active reservations, invalidates catalog/inventory sync queries, and has focused API/store tests. importance: high — note: ← WI-38921 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Implement the Studio secondary tab navigation and Inventory panel by reusing the Event Manager catalog filters and InventoryPickerGrid, with selectable variants, editable price/quantity, mutation feedback, and focused web tests. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-38925 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Run focused and full SideStage verification, browser-drive Current event → Event manager → Inventory, capture final screenshots, and close the plan with evidence. importance: high blocked-by: P-002, P-004 — note: ← WI-38932 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Move Held items into the global top navbar immediately left of Ready for your next event; move one shared Demo user control immediately right of the Android download CTA; remove Watch/Studio-local identity controls; preserve role-specific transport identities behind one visible persona and verify responsive behavior. importance: high — note: ← WI-38924 completed (done)\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Restock extends the existing inventory authority\nDate: 2026-08-14\nThe add-inventory write runs through AuctionInventory/InventoryController. It increments qty atomically and never resets reserved_qty, so active cart/event/auction holds survive stock intake. Catalog reads observe the same storefront_product row in Postgres; the in-memory fallback mirrors the mutation through its existing fixture source rather than inventing a second store.\nRelated: P-001\n\n### D-002 — Inventory is a peer Studio subtab\nDate: 2026-08-14\nStudio exposes exactly three secondary tabs in order: Current event, Event manager, Inventory. Current event hosts the live dock workspace; Event manager hosts the existing setup/queue pane; Inventory hosts the new full-width intake workflow. The main global Studio tab and Ticket chrome remain unchanged.\nRelated: P-002\n\n### D-003 — Reuse the catalog grid by parameterizing semantics\nDate: 2026-08-14\nInventory reuses InventoryPickerGrid and the existing catalog/filter primitives. Any label/action differences are expressed by props or a thin host component; no duplicated table, checkbox, filter, or draft-state implementation is allowed.\nRelated: P-002\n\n### D-004 — Owner-required Studio tab order supersedes D-002\nDate: 2026-08-14\nDate: 2026-08-14\nOwner Avi explicitly requires the three Studio secondary tabs, left to right, to be Inventory, Event Manager, Active Event. This decision supersedes D-002's prior Current event / Event manager / Inventory ordering and naming. Active Event remains the URL/default view unless the owner separately changes the default; visual order is exact.\nRelated: P-002\n",
